   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HelpAge International</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Comprehensive Model for Community Resilience in Vietnam (Phase 4)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide training for older people (Association of the Elderly) on CBDRM/A: these trainings will be provided by HelpAge International in Vietnam (HAIV) at national and provincial levels to ensure basic understanding are provided for older people before they join the comprehensive trainings on CBDRM/A, and empower them to join later interventions)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Raise awareness on older people (vulnerability, capacities, needs and contributions, and the way to work with older people) for local partners, TSG members, and other relevant stakeholders: this intervention will be provided by HAIV at all target provinces either through trainings or dissemination of OP leaflets.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of the Activity is to ensure targeted communities, schools and its diverse groups are more resilient to multi-hazards through reinforcing structure, enhancing capacity, optimizing resources on preparedness and response at community level, supported by influencing the relevant regulatory environments for disaster risk management at national and sub-national levels. This can be achieved through the purpose of having the target communities, including schools, built their knowledge of disaster risks, self-organized and taken individual and collective actions to establish a culture of preparedness and response, and reinforced their networks and connectedness by the end of the Activity. This purpose can be met if communities and schools are prepared and ready to respond to natural hazards and disasters with support of capacitated relevant agencies</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Train the TSG members on how to include older people on the CBDRM program: This training will be provided by HAIV at all target provinces to ensure TSG members can know how to use the OP inclusion checklist that was developed in the previous Consortium phases.</narrative>
  </description>
